> What is a general strategy I might employ for finding altars? I've only been
> up to sokoban so far, and have had trouble finding altars that I can safely
> convert. Should I just go ahead and convert the one in minetown if I haven't
> found one by the time I've reached sokoban? Thanks for any suggestions.

There is no strategy for that as one cannot affect the random generation 
of altars in the dungeons.

There are guaranteed altars in the game though. You've alrady found out 
that there is one in minetown, there are others on the various quests.

My suggestion is to go down. Try to find an unattended altar lower in 
the main dungeon. Sometimes even that won't help and you have to fight 
the priest of a shrine.

To do that more safely dug out a wall (and part of the surrounding area 
if necessary) of the shrine. Then stay outside the shrine area when 
attacking the priest with ranged weapons. The priest won't come out of 
the shrine and his god won't try to fry you. Be ready to fight a demon, 
an angel or an elemental when you convert the altar as desecration of a 
shrine will lead into a retaliation from the former god.

You also could use beefed up pet to get rid of the priest, but you still 
have to be ready when converting the altar.

